hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2740","**\nNarrated to us Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī, narrated to us Sufyān, from Hishām ibn Ḥujayr, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), who said:\n\"The *Ḥijr* is part of the House, because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed *ṭawāf* around the House from behind it. And Allah, the Exalted, said: *'And let them perform *ṭawāf* around the Ancient House.'* (Qur'an 22:29)\"\n\nAbū Bakr (RA) said:\n\"This statement, 'The *Ḥijr* is part of the House,' is of the same type as I have explained in other places in our books: that a noun preceded by the definite article *al-* may refer to a part of something. The Prophet (ﷺ) commanded ʿĀʾishah (RA) to pray within the *Ḥijr*, and he (ﷺ) said: *'The *Ḥijr* is part of the House,'* intending a part of it, not all of it. And Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), may Allah have mercy on him, did not mean by his statement, 'The *Ḥijr* is part of the House,' that the entire *Ḥijr* is part of the House. Rather, he meant a part of it, as informed by ʿĀʾishah (RA) from the Prophet (ﷺ): that a part of the *Ḥijr* is part of the House, not all of it.\"\n\n---"
